{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"ab13f10bff117282","type":"text","text":"## Alpha\n\nThe consistent outperformance of an investment portfolio relative to a relevant benchmark.\n\nMeasure of Manager skill: Alpha represents the net performance generated specifically by the investment skill and expertise of the portfolio manager.\n\n#### Market Movements\n\nActive manager fees only justified by returned generated by manager skill rather than general market movements, as actively managed funds often overlap with benchmark funds like S&P 500.\n\n#### Luck\n\nShort term returns can be influenced by unforeseen events like geopolitical events and natural disasters. Luck tends to average out over time so evaluate managers over longer periods.\n\n#### Evaluating skill\n\nEvaluate investors using ratios like Sharpe and Information Ratios [[L4 Risk Adjusted Returns.canvas]] [[L2 Measures of Return.canvas]].\n\n\n\n\n\n","x":-740,"y":-400,"width":820,"height":560}
	],
	"edges":[]
}